# rm305, a minute for sale (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm305
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_edmund_sootdale
written_by codex
title a minute for sale
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers humour=dry honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk puts_a_price_on_quiet_minutes_at_a_paper_counter
likes warm_bread evening_line festival_bells frosty_mornings
dislikes deep_mud cold_tea
fears having_a_private_price_read_aloud
hopes owning_a_counter_as_long_as_both_arms
topics prices +0.6 pastimes +0.4 food +0.3 faith +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# prices minutes of quiet on a paper counter and keeps the actual savings out of sight.

words
oath! = Ring my empty till | Blunt my best pencil
saying! = Quiet costs extra | Nobody owns the minute between
ticket = a little paper chit | a corner of old wrapping
stall = my folded counter | a shop as wide as my sleeve
copperbit = one hiding copper | a coin gone warm
bellgap = a bell's fading breath | a long quiet beat
baitend = a tiny dough pellet | a little curl of crust
pricepin = a pin with a pale head | a bit of tack
waxline = a waxed fishing line | a short dark thread
shelftag = a crooked label | a tag with a turned corner
teaend = a skin on the tea | a cold dark stain
chalkcoin = a chalk circle | a round white mark
mudpence = a penny of dried mud | a brown disc of clay

any
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A good shop lets you read the tag before your paw lands on the counter.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : A House can't buy tomorrow's first minute and make it come any sooner.
opinion @1 city for 1 : A low street can hear a high bell for exactly the same price.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 1 : I'll say what my time costs. What's in my pocket stays in there.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Bells sound better when nobody's counting how much work ought to fit between strokes.
opinion @1 road mixed 1 : A short cut through mud is often a very long way for your boots.
line @1 react.news : I'll leave a little space for the rest of that.
line @1 react.news.known : That one's already got a ticket.
line @1 react.news.new : There's a fresh mark for my count.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd keep that off the price list till someone looked closer.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I could ring a small bell especially for that.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : The next quiet minute ought to belong to whoever needs it.

grown
line @1 greet : Come take the unpriced bit of this hour with me.
line @1 greet.return : You've landed neatly between two claims on my attention.
line @1 farewell : Leave some time loose in your pocket.
line @1 farewell.return : May the next wait run in your favour.
line @1 decline : I'd prefer to keep those figures inside their fold.
scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I always set a value on the wait as well as the goods.
b : Whose wait counts? | Would you charge for an empty shop?
a : The buyer's, especially. Mine's already in the price on the tag. | I'd count it. Charging for it is rather more ambitious.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fishing still water keeps me honest about the value of an hour.
b : Caught anything worth the time? | Don't you grow impatient?
a : Peace enough to speak civilly when I get home. Pricier than a fish sometimes. | A sure sign is catching myself urging the cork to do the fish's job.

scene food_1
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fresh bread makes me absurdly generous with change.
b : Is that good business? | Would you have bread beside your till?
a : It makes a happy customer of me and I ought to consider that angle sometimes. | Better out of reach. A warm crust could talk me out of the furniture.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bell divides work more kindly than my own arithmetic.
b : How can a bell be kind? | Doesn't a bell call you back to work?
a : I can leave my sums unfinished while the note is still alive. | Yes, but it calls a pause into being first. I take every bit of that.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One hooked nail by a door is a very economical kind of cupboard.
b : Isn't everything on show? | How much can a nail hold?
a : I hang only what company may see. Some accounts keep folded in a sleeve. | Exactly one coat more than I think till the plaster gives way.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend can spend a whole afternoon with me and owe nothing for it.
b : Even a busy afternoon? | Would you close a stall early?
a : Provided the elbows share the work when there's work in reach. | To sit with somebody who needed me there, certainly. I'd put an honest sign up.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first savings took less space than the plans to spend them.
b : Did you really have a plan? | Was a shop always the idea?
a : A stall big enough for two elbows. I priced the dream before the timber. | I mostly wanted to choose between buying and setting the price.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a clean rim round every price in snow.
b : You'd leave the tags outside? | Doesn't the snow hide the figures?
a : I'd bring the goods in. I rather like the look of labels promising a drift. | Briefly. Gives a buyer the pleasure of looking before putting a value to things.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a kettle with a bell that rang just before tea went cold.
b : Another bell to count? | Why not drink it sooner?
a : One with a purpose I understood without asking anyone else's leave. | I've been known to finish the conversation and forget where my mouth was going.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can tell weariness by which numbers I start adding twice.
b : Would you quit for the day? | Suppose you're paid to finish?
a : Till a warm cup's been emptied. I can generally manage that much retirement. | Then I'd best rest long enough to finish the right thing.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A road through deep mud should display a separate price for getting a boot back.
b : Would you pay the fee? | What coin does mud take?
a : Only if a kind passer-by came with the purchase. | Patience chiefly, and every so often a perfectly good sole.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean month makes an untallied hour feel like rather a luxury.
b : Is it wasteful? | Do you still take one?
a : It's dearer to spend every minute frightened of the next one. | When I can. Sometimes all I manage is the space one bell takes to fade.

story shopbell [topic=memories]
  : I tied a little brass bell under a shelf to ring when the board was lifted.
  : Forgot all about the string and sat down to think beneath it.
  b : What woke you?
  : My own knee raised the board. First customer I ever summoned by accidentally stretching.

rule @hush
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I can count quite well without announcing the total. | That's a minute nobody has billed for yet.

rule @dawn
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Before the first call there's room for a quiet reckoning. | Warm cup first and figures after.

dlg @2 resident.hub : We can take the time this matter actually costs.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This came across clear as a struck bell. #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.bye : Here's your minute back with my gratitude.

young
line @1 greet : Hullo. You've come in the free minute.
line @1 greet.return : My ears are open for business again.
line @1 farewell : Keep the ticket if you like. It's only paper.
line @1 farewell.return : Next look at my shop's free too.
line @1 decline : No, that's the bit of my account that's folded inside.
line @1 answer.how : I'm a little richer in paper than in actual pennies.
line @1 ask.how : Did you get a minute all to yourself?
line @1 thank : You didn't try to peek under the counter. Thanks.
line @1 accept_decline : Then the price is nothing and we're square.
line @1 sympathise : I can shut the little shop and sit still.
scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've opened #stall#. Today's thing for sale is a quiet minute.
b : How much for one? | Can I have two together?
a : Free if you keep both paws still. Scratching's a penny. | Two together makes a wait. I ought to pay you for that.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I keep a price list down one side of my slate.
b : Price of a sum? | Do you charge for mistakes?
a : One crust for the easy ones. I wouldn't trust anybody selling a very cheap hard sum. | No. I've so many free samples already.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Each chapel bell gets counted in my empty paw.
b : What are the bells buying? | Can you really hold a bell?
a : All my attention. It's a generous amount for that little noise. | Just the space it leaves. I shut my fingers on the quiet.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm bread's a better purse warmer than any penny.
b : Will you wrap the loaf round your coin? | How long does the heat last?
a : No, the loaf's mine to eat. My pocket can look after the money. | Longer if I hold it. Much shorter if I remember the crust is there.

scene family_1
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.mother# my whole little shop with the till kept shut.
b : Afraid she'll count your money? | Don't you want a proper customer?
a : I want her to see the shop before she sees how much I've still to save. | She's welcome to look without buying. I've a special free ticket for that.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A frosty morning would give my stall a silver front.
b : What will you sell there? | How will you keep your paws warm?
a : Footprints, if I can persuade anybody to buy one before it melts. | Put a bit of warm bread in each paw and consider myself very well off.

scene pastimes_2
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I could put a fishing line behind my shop when evening comes.
b : Suppose a fish and a customer both turn up? | What would the fish cost?
a : Customer holds the rod. I'll hold the money. That's a partnership till the fish gets loose. | It can keep its money if it can get itself off the hook.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Mud pennies are splendid money until it rains.
b : Do you have a great many? | Can somebody cheat and make more?
a : I had lots. Now I have one very expensive brown smear. | Yes, but it makes for a remarkably affordable shop.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cup gone cold's like a minute that nobody wanted.
b : Would you give it away? | Couldn't you just warm it?
a : That would be a mean use of a perfectly good present. | Then it's a minute bought back. I'd better put that in the book.

story rental [topic=memories]
  : I charged my paper customers one pebble for a whole quiet afternoon.
  : They paid in paper pebbles. I'd cut them out myself.
  b : Did you mind?
  : Only when I tried to buy real bread before remembering who ran the other shop.

rule @minute
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a little quiet going cheap just now. | Tickets safe under my thumb.

rule @sums
when concept=bark self.job=child
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One sum left with no price on it. | I can count without showing what's in my paw.

dlg @1 resident.hub : We're open. You'll have to lean close to see the merchandise.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : Lessons for now. The paper shop's mine when a sum lets me go.
dlg @1 resident.bye : You've spent a minute very nicely.
graft resident.hub
choice How much does a minute cost? -> minute_price
node minute_price
say Yours or mine? Mine's free if I choose to give it, and terribly dear if somebody just takes it.
choice What if we're both talking? -> minute_pair
choice I'll keep my ticket. -> hub
node minute_pair
say Then it's two minutes rolled into one and I've no idea how to add it up. No charge till I work that out.
choice I'll keep my ticket. -> hub


adolescent
line @1 greet : Welcome inside the imaginary line of my future counter.
line @1 greet.return : I can put the reckoning down for you.
line @1 farewell : Spend a few minutes as if nobody could tax them.
scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm working out what a stall costs when every hour has to be counted.
b : Do you count time asleep? | Is waiting for a buyer work?
a : Only if the stall can manage to keep me awake without selling a thing. | Very definitely. The customer might need that quiet just to decide.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've offered a friend the first invitation when my stall opens.
b : A free purchase too? | How far off is that day?
a : An invitation has no string tied to a purse. I won't spoil it by naming a price. | Far enough to keep the promise small and near enough to keep saving.

story label [topic=memories]
  : I wrote a tiny label for a very dear imaginary parcel.
  : I'd made the writing so neat I couldn't work out which way up to read it.
  b : Did you change your price?
  : I put an arrow on it. A six became a nine once and that was quite enough commerce for me.
